eeds facts from a stream is not a middleware: folding a stream is an\\ninterpreter's work, and what a middleware reads is a decision an\\ninterpreter already published onto a medium.\\n| 5  | REPL as a service: `yin.repl.serve` and `connect` over     | `(connect \\\"daostream:ws://...\\\")` resolves to a remote        | clj cljs cljd |\\n|    | `requests` and `answers` reflections; delete               | descriptor pair; the demo REPLs work; `yin.repl.link` serves |               |\\n|    | `dao.stream.serving`, `dao.stream.rpc.ws`, the apply wire  | content through slice 4; `dao.stream.rpc` is reworked over   |               |\\n|    | envelope from `dao.stream.apply`; rework or retire         | reflections or retired in the same slice, because the apply  |               |\\n|    | `dao.stream.rpc`.                                          | envelope it requires is deleted here.                        |               |\\n+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\\n| 6  | UDP channel: `dao.stream.udp` with fragmentation keyed by  | The toy over UDP with a 48 KiB value (inside the default    | clj cljs cljd |\\n|    | attachment, address, direction and id; adapters            | 64 KiB maximum); loss injection recovers by resend;         |               |\\n|    | `src/clj/dao/stream/udp/jvm.clj`, `src/cljs/dao/           | oversize beyond the maximum answers `transport-error`       |               |\\n|    | stream/udp/node.cljs`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/udp/dart.cljd`.| with reason `oversize`.                                     |               |\\n+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\\n| 7  | Pair channel and the meeting and relay conventions with    | Two peers behind a simulated restricted NAT punch; behind    | clj           |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-26 21:41:11 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 04:41:11 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\nThe 48 KiB UDP proof, plan section 2 pointer, middleware exceptions, and remote-spec wraps are present. The wraps introduced no defect I could identify. Two findings remain:\\n\\nP2 | [dao.stream.middleware.md:90](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:90) | The prohibition says a cursor is “re-mint[ed] after a gap,” but the gate’s gap rule adopts a recovery cursor and re-reads once; cursor minting is retried after other non-`ok` outcomes ([line 138](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:138), [line 143](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md:143)). The following parenthetical is also duplicated. | Replace both parentheticals with one sentence that distinguishes gap recovery from cursor re-minting and states that neither retries the wrapped operation.\\n\\nP3 | [dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:109](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:109) | The edited slice 6 rows are 145 columns while the surrounding table rules and rows are 146, leaving the right border misaligned. | Pad the slice 6 cells to the table’s existing width.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":163636,\"cached_input_tokens\":126208,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1565,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":204}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
